vies and was even  referenced in a 2003 speech by former  venezuelan president hugo chavez  el silbon has left his impact on popular  culture  but that doesn't mean this monster has  lost his influence in the annos  even young people who sometimes laugh  about it or makes jokes about  the appearance of a silvan when you ask  them seriously  they say they fear him that they can  hear his whistle  at night in the town i believe that  telling the legends  and the tradition of a culture is a way  to preserve an identity  i think it's important to understand  what's cursed us  while it's in the shadow when it's here  today the myth of el silbon is an active  part of the folklore of the janos  continuing a tradition hundreds of years  [Music]  old  you

